# 10 Extended character classes: (?[ ... ]) set operations
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2pattern.html
#
# Needs PCRE2 10.45 or newer. PHP bundles 10.44, where the pattern below
# fails to compile ("unrecognized character after (? or (?-").
#
# What it is: Perl-style extended classes with real set algebra inside
# the pattern. & is intersection, | is union, - is subtraction and ^ is
# symmetric difference. Parentheses and free whitespace are allowed.
# 10.45 also added PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS, which puts the UTS#18
# operators (&&, --, ~~) inside ordinary [...] classes. That variant is an
# API option, so PHP would additionally need a new modifier for it.
#
# What it enables: classes computed from properties instead of
# hand-built ranges. "Letters that are ASCII" or "everything Greek except
# vowels" without enumerating code points.

# Expect: 0: x
# Intersection: a letter that is also ASCII.
/(?[ \p{L} & \p{ASCII} ])/utf
    x

# Expect: No match
# é is a letter but not ASCII, so the intersection excludes it.
/(?[ \p{L} & \p{ASCII} ])/utf
    é

# Expect: 0: x
# The same intersection in UTS#18 spelling inside plain brackets. Enabled
# by the PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS compile option (alt_extended_class here).
/[\p{L} && \p{ASCII}]/utf,alt_extended_class
    x
